# Agent workflow

## Default scope is narrow
- Treat **@mentioned paths**, the **active editor**, and **paths named in the prompt** as the work surface. Do not list or read the whole tree to satisfy a local edit.
- Find symbols with **grep or scoped search** (prefer a single directory), then **read only relevant files** — small ranges when possible.

## Design vs implementation
- **Claude** owns product/UX exploration; **Cursor** implements against a **stable brief** in the repo when possible.
- Ask the user to **@mention one doc** per feature (e.g. `docs/design/...` or a short spec under `docs/`) instead of rediscovering requirements by scanning the codebase.

## Heavy references only when the task needs them
- Do not open long design dumps or prototypes unless the task is **UI, layout, or theming** (see `design-system.mdc` globs).

## For the human (habit)
- After design in Claude: paste a **short implementation checklist** into **one file** and @mention it once in Cursor for each chunk of work — avoids repeating context and avoids model-led “tour of the repo.”
